## 7. Compare Failed and Successful Logins

Search both types of events:

```bash
sudo grep -E "Failed password|Accepted password|Accepted publickey" \
/var/log/auth.log | tail -n 50
```

Look for patterns such as:

```text
00:15:01 — Failed login
00:15:05 — Failed login
00:15:09 — Failed login
00:16:00 — Successful login
```

This is an illustrative timeline.

If you find this pattern in your logs, check whether the successful event involves the same account, source IP, and relevant time window.

A successful login after repeated failures can be important, but it may also be legitimate activity. Validate the context before drawing a conclusion.

