## 8. Monitor Sudo Activity

Unexpected privileged activity may be relevant after an unusual login.

Search the authentication log:

```bash
sudo grep "sudo" /var/log/auth.log | tail -n 30
```

Look for details such as:

- User who invoked `sudo`
- Command executed
- Timestamp
- Whether the action was expected

Remember that `sudo` activity does not automatically indicate malicious behavior. Administrators and normal users may use it legitimately.

---

## 9. Check Recent Login Sessions

Run:

```bash
who
```

Displays currently logged-in users.

```bash
w
```

Displays logged-in users and session activity.

```bash
last -n 20
```

Displays recent login records when the system has the relevant accounting data.

These commands provide different perspectives. Current sessions and historical login records may not contain every detail required to reconstruct an incident.

