## 10. Generate a Safe Test Event

If SSH is installed and running on your own Ubuntu VM, you can generate a controlled local test event:

```bash
ssh invalid-lab-user@localhost
```

The invalid username should fail to authenticate if it does not exist.

Then inspect the logs:

```bash
sudo grep -Ei "Invalid user|Failed password" /var/log/auth.log | tail -n 10
```

This test may generate an invalid-user event rather than a failed-password event, depending on the SSH server configuration.

Do not use password-guessing tools or test against systems you do not own or have explicit authorization to assess.

