### Challenge questions

**Q1. Which Linux file commonly stores Ubuntu authentication logs?**

`/var/log/auth.log`

**Q2. Does a high failed-login count prove brute force?**

No. The source, time window, targeted accounts, and surrounding activity must be investigated.

**Q3. Why investigate a successful login after repeated failures?**

It may be related to the preceding failures and deserves validation against the same account, source, and timeline.

**Q4. What does `uniq -c` do in the source-IP pipeline?**

It counts adjacent identical lines. Sorting the addresses first groups identical values together.

**Q5. Why analyze original logs as well as Wazuh alerts?**

Original logs help validate the event details and distinguish a missing collection or detection problem from the absence of the underlying event.

